ranscript, provided it contains the details of the study records. 4. Details of one referee Provide the name, position, organisation, and contact details of one referee. 5. Any other relevant supporting documents that may influence the filling of the position (optional) Please note that applicants must also complete the DETECTIVE online application form available at virusdetective.eu or Webropol link . Candidates will be shortlisted and invited to participate in a two-stage interview process. The first round of online interviews will be conducted between 30 October and 9 November 2026. Candidates who progress to the next stage will be invited to a second round of interviews during November 2026. The recruitment process is expected to be completed by December 2026. Important Information Regarding Doctoral Study Rights The information in this section applies only to candidates selected for the position and is not required at the application stage. Please note that employment cannot commence on 1 March 2027 unless the selected candidate has been granted the right to pursue doctoral studies at the University of Turku. Admission to doctoral studies is a prerequisite for employment. You must meet the faculty and doctoral programme requirements for granting the right to pursue a doctoral degree. Carefully read the application guidelines of the Medical Faculty and the requirements of the Turku Doctoral Programme of Molecular Medicine . Applicants selected for the position will be required to prepare, together with their supervisors, the documents necessary for the doctoral study right application, including: Supervision and study plan – the Faculty’s form (Fill in electronically, print and sign together with the supervisor/-s and the head of subject, see: Subjects in doctoral training and heads of doctoral subject ). ​​​​​​ Please refer to the faculty website for more detailed instructions. Research plan (maximum three pages , excluding references; Arial, font size 12). The