    "https://ats.talentadore.com/apply/kehityspaallikko-tai-projektikoordinaattori-kaupallistaminen-materiaalitekniikka/Zy17y7?lang=en&UTUID=21685": {
      "title": "Development Manager or Project Coordinator (Commercialization), Materials Engineering",
      "description": "Development Manager or Project Coordinator (Commercialization), Materials Engineering | Department of Mechanical and Materials Engineering JavaScript is disabled. Please enable JavaScript for the best recruiting experience. Apply for this position Development Manager or Project Coordinator (Commercialization), Materials Engineering University of Turku is a world-class multidisciplinary research university offering challenging work and a unique perspective on Finnish and international research and education. The Materials in Health Technology and Flexible Devices research group at the Department of Mechanical and Materials Engineering, University of Turku, is seeking a Development Manager / Project Coordinator to work on commercialization in the ChiralNanoDetect project funded by the Academy of Finland. The position starts as soon as possible or upon mutual agreement. Part-time work is possible; in that case the employment period will be agreed separately (e.g., 12 months). As a full-time position, the duration is 6 months. The project ends on 31 December 2027. The successful candidate will be expected to assess the commercial potential of the sensor technology and help build a pathway towards commercialization. This includes conducting market and competitor analyses, identifying potential end-users and industrial partners, engaging with clinicians and other stakeholders, supporting the IP and patentability assessment, and contributing to a commercialization roadmap covering further development, regulatory requirements, funding opportunities, and potential routes such as licensing or a spin-out. The specifics of the task will be determined based on the selected candidate's experience. Who we are looking for Requirements A relevant higher university degree (Master’s level) Excellent English skills; knowledge of Finnish is considered an advantage. Strong communication skills; ability to work with both researchers and external stakeholders. Previous experience in technology commercialization, market analyses, business development or related fields. Familiarity with medical devices, diagnostics, intellectual property, regulatory requirements, or early-stage technology development is considered as advantage. Project management experience is also appreciated. We value collegiality and promote equality, diversity, and inclusivity. We encourage all qualified applicants with different backgrounds to apply for our open positions. Benefits The Unit of Materials Engineering offers a young and dynamic community. We support team players to reach their best potential and we give the opportunity to develop your professional skills in a diverse operating environment. We support your efforts for reaching excellence and we are committed to taking care of your well-being at work and the functionality of your daily life, e.g. flexible working hours and our welfare services. Possibilities to develop your expertise – We encourage our personnel to develop their professional expertise by offering versatile training and competence development possibilities which employees can take advantage of during their working hours. Also, the course offering of Open University is free of charge for our personnel. Your well-being is important to us! – In addition to comprehensive occupational health care, our own well-being services monitor, support and develop the well-being of our personnel. You are entitled to use the CampusSport’s services at a personnel price. We support your work-life balance – Flexible working hours and extensive remote work options help you balance work and leisure time. An inspiring and supportive work community – We encourage each other and value working together! Please read more about University of Turku as an employer from our Come work with us! pages. The European Commission has awarded the University of Turku the right to use the HR Excellence in Research quality label . The label is a token of the University's commitment to continuous development of the position and working conditions of researchers according to the guidelines set forth in the European Charter for Researchers. The University of Turku is among the top of the world’s universities in most rankings and among the best universities in the world in certain fields. Our high-quality basic research, a multidisciplinary research profile and close cooperation in research infrastructures creates the basis for international top research. Read more about University of Turku in international university rankings. The University of Turku has several high-quality research infrastructures required for cutting-edge research. Learn more about the roadmap of research infrastructures and how the research infrastructure and expert teams offer tailored solutions for businesses and organizations . Salary and trial period The salary is determined in accordance with the university salary system for other staff member group (collective agreement of universities). The demand level of the salary is 9-10, in addition a personal performance percentage will be paid. Depending on previous experience and competence, the starting salary for a full-time appointment is approx. 3700–4200€ per month. There is a trial period determined in the contracts of employment act. How to apply Applications must be submitted by Fri 16th of October, 2026 (16:00) using the electronic application form of the University of Turku on the following address: https://www.utu.fi/en/university/come-work-with-us/open-vacancies. The link to the application system is at the beginning of this announcement (Apply for the job). Applications should include: CV, Motivation letter (a description of your expertise in the field and your suitability for this position, please mention also are you interested in the part-time or full-time working time), Contact details of two referees, Copies of degree certificates, and other documents (eg. list of publications) that might be relevant to the call. Further information For further information, please contact Prof. Emilia Peltola (emilia.peltola(at)utu.fi). For questions related to the application process, please contact HR specialist Janna Salminen (jansaly(at)utu.fi). Apply between and Department of Mechanical and Materials Engineering Department of Mechanical and Materials Engineering is a unique combination of mechanical engineering, materials engineering and industrial engineering and management with contemporary research and teaching. Our vision is to create trends. We take the needs of the community, business, society and the environment into account when actively guiding our activities in teaching, research and collaboration. The Faculty of Technology is the newest faculty of the University of Turku, it was established in the beginning of 2021. The Faculty consists of the Department of Computing, Department of Biotechnology and the Department of Mechanical and Materials Engineering. We have more than 2,500 graduate and postgraduate students and circa 600 employees, of whom more than 50 are professors. Our faculty is an international, multicultural and diverse work community. The University of Turku is an inspiring and international academic community of 25,000 students and staff in Southwest Finland. We build a sustainable future with multidisciplinary research, education, and collaboration. With us, your work will have a significant impact and relevance in the changing world. See our open vacancies Homepage LinkedIn Facebook Youtube Instagram Information for the applicant The application form cannot be saved as a draft. However, after submitting you can return to edit your application via the link you receive by email. The application can be edited until the application deadline. You have 6 hours to complete your application before the timeout. Instructions for submitting a job application Apply for this position English Suomi English Development Manager or Project Coordinator (Commercialization), Materials Engineering Add your picture Are you sure you want to withdraw this application? Would you like to tell us the reason for this withdrawal? Back to form Saving changes Saved!"
